"GitHub - QwenLM/Qwen3-VL: Qwen3-VL is the multimodal large language model series developed by Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud. · GitHub (https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-VL)\nciteturn2880view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-VL\",\"pattern\":\"2025.10\"}); Total lines: 1213\nL171: ## Introduction\nL172: \nL173: Meet Qwen3-VL — the most powerful vision-language model in the Qwen series to date.\nL174: \nL176: Available in Dense and MoE architectures that scale from edge to cloud, with Instruct and reasoning‑enhanced Thinking editions for flexible, on‑demand deployment.\nL177: #### Key Enhancements:\nL178: \nL179:   * Visual Agent: Operates PC/mobile GUIs—recognizes elements, understands functions, invokes tools, completes tasks.\nL180: \nL181:   * Visual Coding Boost: Generates Draw.io/HTML/CSS/JS from images/videos.\nL182: \nL183:   * Advanced Spatial Perception: Judges object positions, viewpoints, and occlusions; provides stronger 2D grounding and enables 3D grounding for spatial reasoning and embodied AI.\nL184:   * Long Context & Video Understanding: Native 256K context, expandable to 1M; handles books and hours-long video with full recall and second-level indexing.\nL185: \nL186:   * Enhanced Multimodal Reasoning: Excels in STEM/Math—causal analysis and logical, evidence-based answers.\nL187: \nL188:   * Upgraded Visual Recognition: Broader, higher-quality pretraining is able to “recognize everything”—celebrities, anime, products, landmarks, flora/fauna, etc.\nL189:   * Expanded OCR: Supports 32 languages (up from 10); robust in low light, blur, and tilt; better with rare/ancient characters and jargon; improved long-document structure parsing.\nL190: \nL191:   * Text Understanding on par with pure LLMs: Seamless text–vision fusion for lossless, unified comprehension.\nL192: #### Model Architecture Updates:\nL193: \nL194:   1. Interleaved-MRoPE: Full‑frequency allocation over time, width, and height via robust positional embeddings, enhancing long‑horizon video reasoning.\nL195: \nL196:   2. DeepStack: Fuses multi‑level ViT features to capture fine‑grained details and sharpen image–text alignment.\nL197: \nL198:   3. Text–Timestamp Alignment: Moves beyond T‑RoPE to precise, timestamp‑grounded event localization for stronger video temporal modeling.\nL199: ## News\nL200:   * 2025.11.27: We have released the cite86†Qwen3-VL paper†arxiv.org , which introduces many technical details about Qwen3-VL, and we hope it will be helpful to everyone.\nL201:   * 2025.10.21: We have released the Qwen3-VL-2B (cite92†Instruct†huggingface.co /cite93†Thinking†huggingface.co ) and Qwen3-VL-32B (cite94†Instruct†huggingface.co /cite95†Thinking†huggingface.co ). Enjoy it!\nL202:   * 2025.10.15: We have released the Qwen3-VL-4B (cite96†Instruct†huggingface.co /cite97†Thinking†huggingface.co ) and Qwen3-VL-8B (cite98†Instruct†huggingface.co /cite99†Thinking†huggingface.co ). Enjoy it!\nL203:   * 2025.10.4: We have released the cite100†Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct†huggingface.co and cite101†Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Thinking†huggingface.co . We have also released the FP8 version of the Qwen3-VL models — available in our cite83†HuggingFace collection†huggingface.co and cite84†ModelScope collection†modelscope.cn .\nL204:   * 2025.09.23: We have released the cite102†Qwen3-VL-235B-A22B-Instruct†huggingface.co and cite103†Qwen3-VL-235B-A22B-Thinking†huggingface.co . For more details, please check our cite85†blog†qwen.ai !\nL205:   * 2025.04.08: We provide the cite104†code for fine-tuning Qwen2-VL and Qwen2.5-VL.\nL206:   * 2025.03.25: We have released the cite105†Qwen2.5-VL-32B†huggingface.co . It is smarter and its responses align more closely with human preferences. For more details, please check our cite106†blog†qwenlm.github.io !\nL207:   * 2025.02.20: we have released the cite107†Qwen2.5-VL Technical Report†arxiv.org . Alongside the report, we have also released AWQ-quantized models for Qwen2.5-VL in three different sizes: cite108†3B†huggingface.co , cite109†7B†huggingface.co , and cite110†72B†huggingface.co parameters.\nL208:   * 2025.01.28: We have released the cite111†Qwen2.5-VL series†huggingface.co . For more details, please check our cite112†blog†qwenlm.github.io !\nL209:   * 2024.12.25: We have released the cite113†QvQ-72B-Preview†huggingface.co . QvQ-72B-Preview is an experimental research model, focusing on enhancing visual reasoning capabilities. For more details, please check our cite114†blog†qwenlm.github.io !\nL210:   * 2024.09.19: The instruction-tuned cite115†Qwen2-VL-72B model†huggingface.co and its quantized version [cite116†AWQ†huggingface.co , cite117†GPTQ-Int4†huggingface.co , cite118†GPTQ-Int8†huggingface.co ] are now available. We have also released the cite119†Qwen2-VL paper†arxiv.org simultaneously.\nL211:   * 2024.08.30: We have released the cite120†Qwen2-VL series†huggingface.co . The 2B and 7B models are now available, and the 72B model for open source is coming soon. For more details, please check our cite121†blog†qwenlm.github.io !\nL212: ## Performance\nL213: \nL214: ### Visual Tasks\nL215: \nL216: ### Text-Centric Tasks\nL217: ## Cookbooks\nL218: \nL219: We are preparing cite72†cookbooks for many capabilities, including recognition, localization, document parsing, video understanding, key information extraction, and more. Welcome to learn more!\nL220: Cookbook  | Description  | Open\nL221: --- | --- | ---\nL222: cite122†Omni Recognition | Not only identify animals, plants, people, and scenic spots but also recognize various objects such as cars and merchandise.  |\nL223: cite123†Powerful Document Parsing Capabilities | The parsing of documents has reached a higher level, including not only text but also layout position information and our Qwen HTML format.  |\nL224: cite124†Precise Object Grounding Across Formats | Using relative position coordinates, it supports both boxes and points, allowing for diverse combinations of positioning and labeling tasks.  |\nL225: cite125†General OCR and Key Information Extraction | Stronger text recognition capabilities in natural scenes and multiple languages, supporting diverse key information extraction needs.  |\nL226: cite126†Video Understanding | Better video OCR, long video understanding, and video grounding.  |\nL227: cite127†Mobile Agent | Locate and think for mobile phone control.  |\nL228: cite128†Computer-Use Agent | Locate and think for controlling computers and Web.  |\nL229: cite129†3D Grounding | Provide accurate 3D bounding boxes for both indoor and outdoor objects.  |\nL230: cite130†Thinking with Images | Utilize image_zoom_in_tool and search_tool to facilitate the model’s precise comprehension of fine-grained visual details within images.  |\nL231: cite131†MultiModal Coding | Generate accurate code based on rigorous comprehension of multimodal information.  |\nL232: cite132†Long Document Understanding | Achieve rigorous semantic comprehension of ultra-long documents.  |\nL233: cite133†Spatial Understanding | See, understand and reason about the spatial information  |\nL234: ## Quickstart\nL235: \nL236: Below, we provide simple examples to show how to use Qwen3-VL with 🤖 ModelScope and 🤗 Transformers.\nL237: \nL238:     `# The Qwen3-VL model requires transformers >= 4.57.0\nL239:     pip install \"transformers>=4.57.0\"\nL240:     `\nL241: \nL242: ### 🤖 ModelScope\nL243: \nL244: We strongly advise users especially those in mainland China to use ModelScope. `snapshot_download` can help you solve issues concerning downloading checkpoints.\nL245: ### Using 🤗 Transformers to Chat\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - QwenLM/Qwen3-VL: Qwen3-VL is the multimodal large language model series developed by Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud. · GitHub 